  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A particle (mass =&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;and charge =&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math>) is moving in a region in which&nbsp;there exists a uniform electric field <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;and a uniform magnetic field <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>. At <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, the&nbsp;particle is at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and is moving with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>.&nbsp;After some time, the particle is located at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and has a velocity&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>v</mi><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>, then which of the following is true?</p>\r"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "at the initial moment, the rate of work done by electric field is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mi>a</mi></mfrac></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "at the initial moment, the rate of work done by electric field is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mi>a</mi></mfrac></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>By work energy theorem</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mi>mag</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mi>ele</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>qE</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>mv</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mfrac><msup><mi>mv</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>qa</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>Rate of work done at initial instant&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo></math> power of electric force</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>qE</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mfrac><msup><mi>mv</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mfrac></math></p>"
